accept_seg6 = min(READ_ONCE(net->ipv6.devconf_all->seg6_enabled),
			  READ_ONCE(idev->cnf.seg6_enabled));
Reason:
__in6_dev_get() can return NULL when the device has no IPv6 configuration (e.g., MTU < IPV6_MIN_MTU or after NETDEV_UNREGISTER). Without a NULL check immediately after the assignment, the subsequent dereference of idev (e.g., `idev->cnf.seg6_enabled`) causes a NULL pointer dereference, leading to a kernel crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!idev) {
